id: P-purpose-anchor-recompute
name: Purpose anchor recompute
description: When an edit shifts lines in a file that .purpose aspects anchor (especially the 3,000+ line studio.ts), recompute every affected anchor from the symbol or code it pins, never by adding a line offset. The Paradigm hook's offset refresh mis-placed anchors, and older studio.ts anchors had drifted onto unrelated code, including three ^localhost-only security invariants.
trigger:
  - .purpose anchors
  - anchor drift
  - stale purpose
  - refresh anchors
  - aspect anchors
tags:
  - paradigm
  - purpose
  - anchors
  - drift
symbols:
  - "#cli-studio"
  - ^localhost-only
steps:
  - action: run
    command: git ls-files '*.purpose' | xargs grep -n '<file>:'
    notes: List every anchor into the edited file in EVERY tracked .purpose (root, packages/*, creator/, .claude/ — several can anchor the same code).
  - action: run
    command: git show <pre-change-sha>:<file> | sed -n '<a>p;<b>p'
    notes: "See what each anchor covered before the change, and read the aspect description: the description is the source of truth, and old anchors may already be wrong."
  - action: run
    command: grep -n '<symbol or distinctive line>' <file>
    notes: "Find the code the aspect pins (function, constant, handler) in the current file and set the range to cover it fully: docblock through the closing brace, guard through its return."
  - action: verify
    notes: Print each new range (sed -n 'a,bp') and check it shows the pinned code. Recheck anchors into every other file the PR changed.
recorded_from: "a-atelier PR #22 review, 2026-10-24"
